These are all really good suggestions.  After all, what makes the game too easy
for some is that they are too spoiled with the exact translations of the game's
"cryptic" messages.  Of course, any such changes should be implemented with a
switch - preferably a run-time "option" setting, so less spoiled people can
still have fun.

Having very nearly finished my first 3.1 game, another suggestion as to
reducing the ease of which experienced or spoiled people can win - change the
way donation-generated intrinisc armor class works.  Currently, many know the
exact number of gold pieces one has to part with to get an extra point of AC.
Why not make this a random multiplier?  Thus, players can't get so much AC
(which is the biggest reason the later levels are so easy, IMHO).  They'd have
to donate a _lot_ of gold to be insured the gift, or could gamble with a lesser
amount.

